    src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7ba1565e-ea36-4d8b-b70a-8601ac5e2e9f"
    />
    
    Per-op profile (same topology, steady-state prefill step):
    
    | Op | Before | After | Delta |
    |---|---|---|---|
    | `vllm::maybe_all_gather_and_maybe_unpad` (per call) | 670 us | 367 us
    | -45% |
    |  `vllm::maybe_pad_and_reduce` (per call) | 1.870 ms | 397 us | -78% |
    
    The remaining 367 us per AG call is the collective itself plus host
    framework, confirming the reconstruction overhead (not the collective)
    was what got removed.
    
