    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    No. No config or API change; performance-only, outputs bit-identical.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    - New unit tests in `tests/ut/ops/test_register_custom_ops.py`: uniform
    AG/RS pass-through, dp=1 and dp=2 no-`local_sizes` fast paths, and
    uneven-size cases guarding the unchanged slow path.
    - Trace verification on a steady-state prefill step: after the patch the
    op subtrees no longer contain `aten::cat` / `aten::zeros(fill)` /
    `aten::select` and contain no extra `aten::copy_`; only the collective
    and host framework remain.
    - E2E benchmark above; long-run stability run on the same topology.
    
    Env: 8x Ascend 910B, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash W4A8, TP8/EP8, dp=1, FlashComm
    v1, FULL_DECODE_ONLY. Dataset: 46.5k-token shared prefix + 3.5k random
    suffix, 350 output tokens, concurrency 6, server-side sampling.
    
    | Metric | Before | After | Delta |
